WEBVTT

00:00:04.200 --> 00:00:07.798
App Composer starts with a sentence, not a repository.

00:00:07.798 --> 00:00:14.393
I described the studio I wanted: images, video and sound, with projects I could save and return to.

00:00:14.393 --> 00:00:17.525
Get Ready checked the machine and the accounts.

00:00:17.525 --> 00:00:23.587
Init turned that description into a specification I could read, save, and hand to my agent.

00:00:23.587 --> 00:00:32.914
The agent built this studio on Cloudflare, with its own database, its own storage and its own release, and opened it from the Composer menu.

00:00:32.914 --> 00:00:37.511
Then I made things in it: a still, a clip, a music bed, a storyboard.

00:00:37.511 --> 00:00:44.640
And when I wanted a change, the same agent changed the same application, and every project was still there.

00:00:45.100 --> 00:00:50.575
In the studio, sound is a saved asset, not a soundtrack bolted on afterwards.

00:00:50.575 --> 00:00:56.618
I can choose a bed that fits the cut, order the takes, and render one bounded export.

00:00:56.618 --> 00:01:03.231
Then I changed the studio itself: a new length control, and a storyboard I can edit in place.

00:01:03.231 --> 00:01:08.350
Same application, same projects, and the first cut still in the library.
